  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k+2\\end{aligned}].$ If $u\\cdot v=0$, find the value of $k.$",
  "worked_solution": "Starting from the equation $u\\cdot v=0,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $k$ and then solve for $k$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ 1\\cdot k+3\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-5)+6\\cdot (k+2) & =0 \\\\ k+12-10+6k+12 & =0 \\\\ 7k+14 & =0 \\\\ 7k & =-14 \\\\ k & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $k=-2.$",
